<title>USA: Amoco says to expand Illinois PIA plant.</title>
<headline>Amoco says to expand Illinois PIA plant.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amoco Corp said it plans to expand the capacity of its purified isophthalic acid, or PIA, plant in Joliet, Ill., to 200,000 tons per year from 93,000 tons per year.</p>
<p>The additional PIA capacity is scheduled to come on stream in the first quarter of 1998, Amoco said.</p>
<p>The oil, gas and chemicals concern also said it plans to construct a metaxylene plant in Texas City, Texas, with a manufacturing capacity of 100,000 tons per year.</p>
<p>Costs of the new projects were not disclosed.</p>
</text>
